      "confidence": "low",
      "note": "Best effort, additive only: 'saʿa {h}' (hour word from the locale's own duration data) + 'we <minutes>' using the locale's conjunction ('we nəs' = and a half, already in duration.half). Tens ʿəsra/salasa/arbaʿa/ḥamsa are the Semitic series I believe Tigre uses; 15 written as 'ʿasərte we ḥamməste'. Doubts: whether Tigre uses an Arabic-style 'rubʿ'/'illa' quarter/to idiom instead; whether the existing hour numerals are genuine Tigre (some look Tigrinya-like); romanization kept to match the file. Hour count: Western (Eritrea)."
